From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386/whpx: CPUID cache and topology leaves from the CPU model

WHPX answers every CPUID leaf that is not in its exit list from the host.
With an Intel CPU model on an AMD host (macOS guests), leaf 4 is then empty
and macOS divides by the core counts derived from it (divide error in
cpu_thread_alloc <- smp_init). Leaves 2, 4, 5, 0x80000005 and 0x80000006 now
come from the CPU model, like leaves 1 and 0xb already do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c |   11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
index 113f79a..8bed0ff 100644
--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -3039,9 +3204,14 @@ int whpx_accel_init(AccelState *as, MachineState *ms)
     WHV_PROCESSOR_FEATURES_BANKS processor_features;
     WHV_PROCESSOR_PERFMON_FEATURES perfmon_features;
 
-    UINT32 cpuidExitList[] = {0x0, 0x1, 0x6, 0x7, 0xb, 0xd, 0x14, 0x24, 0x29, 0x1E,
-        0x40000000, 0x40000001, 0x40000010, 0x80000000, 0x80000001,
-        0x80000002, 0x80000003, 0x80000004, 0x80000007, 0x80000008,
+    /*
+     * Leaves 2, 4, 5, 0x80000005 and 0x80000006 (cache and core topology) come from the CPU
+     * model too: with an Intel model on an AMD host the host's answers are empty (leaf 4) or
+     * describe another topology, and macOS divides by the core counts derived from them.
+     */
+    UINT32 cpuidExitList[] = {0x0, 0x1, 0x2, 0x4, 0x5, 0x6, 0x7, 0xb, 0xd, 0x14, 0x24, 0x29,
+        0x1E, 0x40000000, 0x40000001, 0x40000010, 0x80000000, 0x80000001,
+        0x80000002, 0x80000003, 0x80000004, 0x80000005, 0x80000006, 0x80000007, 0x80000008,
         0x8000000A, 0x80000021, 0x80000022, 0xC0000000, 0xC0000001};
 
     X86MachineState *x86ms = X86_MACHINE(ms);
